From: OpenWiFi BCM4360 Project <bcm4360@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH 16/16] brcmfmac: pcie: BCM4360 test.316 R3b novram + console tail + P1-T mirror

Fire #9 (0015) gave two hard facts: (1) R3a -- stripping "boardtype="
from NVRAM -- did NOT move the fw: the console wr_idx stayed at 0x27d
(637), the same stall as in fires #6-#8; (2) P1 -- PLAIN write
MAILBOXINT (BAR0+0x48) := 0xFFFFFFFF before set_active -- read back
0x3 (the write masked down to the two doorbell bits), but AFTER
set_active mbint=0: brcmf_chip_set_active CLEARS the mailbox, so the
frozen fw never saw the doorbell. Kimptoc's intstatus=0x300
(T284-era, pre-set_active) remains the only unexplained observation:
it is either a HW mirror of HIS OWN pre-release write, or a fw-side
latch of an fw that went further (1404 B of console). Three probes in
0016 settle it in a single fire #10:

a) bcm4360_test316=1 (master switch) -- R3b: in
   brcmf_pcie_download_fw_nvram, at the place where NVRAM is written to
   TCM (vars buffer + the end token that lands at TCM[ramsize-4]),
   the WHOLE write branch is SKIPPED: no vars buffer copy, no token;
   the write_ram32(ramsize-4, 0) leaves the sharedram marker at 0 --
   the exact kimptoc test.28 substrate, whose fw had NO NVRAM
   (bmac_attach err 15 -> TRAP) and yet went further than 637 B.
   Guard order: test316 takes precedence over the 0015 strip (R3a) --
   with test316=1 the vars buffer never leaves host RAM, so a strip
   (even if test315 is also set) is moot; the test276 varsz/vars16
   snapshot then reads zeros -- expected (the fw sees the same:
   varsz=0). CPU-only, zero MMIO; the buffer is freed unwritten.

b) P1-T: the 0015 P1 block condition (P3 read-only MAILBOXMASK + P1
   PLAIN write MAILBOXINT := bcm4360_test315_db_val + readback,
   between the INTERNAL_MEM reset and brcmf_chip_set_active, ARM in
   halt) is extended with test316 (bcm4360_test315 || bcm4360_test316);
   the pr_emerg messages are generalized to "test.315/316".
   Immediately AFTER the P1 readback, two single windowed SB-side
   reads (BAR0+0x20 intstatus, BAR0+0x24 intmask), bracketed + a
   "P1-T mirror check: intstatus=... intmask=... mbint=..." line:
   intstatus=0x300 PRE-release (ARM in halt, our P1 just latched
   mbint=0x3) => kimptoc's 0x300 = HW mirror of his own write;
   ~0/0x80 => no mirror -- kimptoc's 0x300 = a fw-side latch, his fw
   went past 637.

c) bcm4360_test316_console_tail=1 (INDEPENDENT of test316 -- works
   with test277=1): in the test.277 POST-POLL block, right after the
   existing console HEAD (first 128 B) dump -- read the LAST
   min(wr_idx, 96) bytes of the console buffer ending at wr_idx
   (guard: wr_idx < 96 -> from 0; wr_idx=0 -> skip with a log). TCM
   read mechanism identical to the HEAD dump
   (brcmf_pcie_read_ram32 into a stack chunk), read start aligned to
   4 B (<=3 B of earlier console text in front; the printed span ends
   exactly at wr_idx), printed as %*ph hex (<=64 B per line, one
   continuation line) + one %*pE line. Invalid struct (buf_addr
   outside TCM, wr_idx > buf_size -- test.278-style validation) ->
   skip with a log. This closes the biggest evidence gap: so far we
   know only the HEAD of the console buffer, and the last fw print
   before the stall is the key (the name of the function where the fw
   got stuck).

d) No other changes: T276/T277/T308/T309/T310/T311/T312/T313/T314/T315
   untouched (the only 0015 touch: extending the P1 block condition +
   generalizing the messages); the 0015 DISCRIMINATOR stays gated on
   test315; gate 0012 and T309 untouched. All parameters default to 0
   -> inert patch.

Safety (imposed by wedges #4/#5): the only new MMIO operations are
(b) two windowed BAR0 PRE-release reads bracketed by pr_emerg
before/after (T305 pre-release WRITE_LANDED + T315 DISCRIMINATOR
class, proven live in #6-#9; stalling reads -- fire ONLY with CTO
10-100 ms) and (c) a loop of <=25 TCM/BAR1 reads
(brcmf_pcie_read_ram32) -- the same class as the existing test.277
HEAD dump (32 reads, survived every fire #6-#9); ZERO new MMIO writes.
R3b is pure CPU (host RAM, zero MMIO; buffer freed). TAIL read start
aligned to 4 B (down), so no misaligned reads; the printed span ends
at wr_idx. test316=0 and test316_console_tail=0 (defaults) => zero
code and behavioural difference (the new parameters are read solely
under their own guards). T309, gate 0012, test313/test314 untouched
(nothing added in teardown).

Requires: test276=1 + test308=1 (full pipeline); test315 and test313
deliberately NOT set in fire #10 (R3a disproved in #9; doorbell-anyway
is a dead path); bcm4360_test315_db_val=0xFFFFFFFF still drives the P1
(-T) write value. Fire only with setpci ASPM-off + CTO 10-100 ms on
the live device.

~160 lines, gated on chip 4360 + test316/test316_console_tail -- zero
behaviour change for every other chip and for the msgbuf path.

Signed-off-by: OpenWiFi BCM4360 Project <bcm4360@localhost>
